# EmailJS — contact form uses POST /api/contact (server-side; private key never goes to the browser).
# Copy to .env.local and fill all values from https://dashboard.emailjs.com/admin
#
# If you only created a Service so far: add an Email Template, link it to that service.
# Subject line: GEN website — {{form_type}} — {{name}}
# Body: copy all HTML from emailjs-contact-template-body.html in this repo into the template editor.
# Set Reply-To to {{reply_to}} in template settings if your provider supports it.
# Put the new template id (e.g. template_abc123) in EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID below.
#
# Template placeholders (match ContactForm / API route):
# {{form_type}} {{name}} {{from_name}} {{email}} {{reply_to}} {{organization}}
# {{job_title}} {{country}} {{program_interest}} {{cohort_size}}
# {{training_objectives}} {{subject}} {{message}}
#
EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
EMAILJS_PRIVATE_KEY=
EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
